\emph{i) Lower bounding the left hand side of \eqref{eq:Pi_apply_Gordon}.}\\
Observe that $\wh{\Delta} \in \mc{T}$ as defined in \eqref{eq:setT}. Moreover, note that under (\text{\textbf{G}}), the random subspace
$\text{range}(X) \subseteq \mathbb{R}^n$ follows the uniform distribution on the Grassmannian $\textsf{G}(n,d)$. Hence, applying Lemma \ref{lem:escape} with $K = \mc{T}$,
$V = \text{range}(X)$ and thus $m = n$ and $l = n-d$, we have for any $\varepsilon \in (0,1/2)$ in compliance with \eqref{eq:cond_samples_unrelaxed}    
\begin{align}\label{eq:lowerbound}
  \begin{split}
   \p(\text{dist}(\mc{T}, \text{range}(X)) > \varepsilon)
   &= \p \left(\min_{\Delta \in \mc{T}} \nnorm{\texttt{P}_X^{\perp} \Delta}_2 > \varepsilon \right) \\
   &\geq 1 - \frac{7}{2} \exp \left(-\frac{1}{2} \left( \frac{(1 - \varepsilon)\nu_{n-d} - \varepsilon \nu_n  - w(\mc{T})}{3 + \varepsilon + \varepsilon \nu_n / \nu_{n-d}} \right)^2 \right) \\
   &\geq 1 - \frac{7}{2} \exp \left(-\frac{\psi(\varepsilon, d/n) \nu_n^2}{8} \right), \quad
   \psi(\varepsilon, d/n) \coloneq \left( \frac{(1- \varepsilon) \frac{\nu_{n-d}}{\nu_n} - \varepsilon}{3 + \varepsilon + \frac{\varepsilon^2}{1-\varepsilon}} \right)^2,
 \end{split}
\end{align}
where the last inequality follows from condition \eqref{eq:cond_samples_unrelaxed}. Conditional on the event $\{ \nnorm{\texttt{P}_X^{\perp} \Delta}_2 \geq \varepsilon \}$, which holds with the probability as stated, the left hand side of \eqref{eq:Pi_apply_Gordon} is lower bounded by $\varepsilon^2 \nnorm{(\wh{\Pi}^{\T}  - \Pi^{*\T}) \mathbf{y}}_2$.  
