\begin{align*}
\p(|\nscp{\texttt{P}_X^{\perp}\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}{\wh{\Delta}}| \geq t) \leq \p \left(\sup_{\Delta \in \mc{T}} |\nscp{\texttt{P}_X^{\perp}\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}{\Delta}| > t \right). 
\end{align*}
\noindent Now note that $\boldsymbol{\epsilon}$ and $\texttt{P}_X^{\perp}$ are independent. As a result, when conditioning on $\texttt{P}_X^{\perp}$, we have from Lemma \ref{lem:concentration_width}
that
\begin{align*}
