                                                                                                           &\leq \exp(-\tau^2 / (2 \sigma^2)),
                                                                                                             \quad \tau \coloneq t - \E\left[\sup_{\Delta \in \mc{T}}  |\nscp{\texttt{P}_X^{\perp}\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}{\Delta}| \;\; \Big|  \texttt{P}_X^{\perp} \right] \\
&\qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \;\; \geq  t - \sigma w(\mc{T}). 
\end{align*}
The second equality is a consequence of the Sudakov-Fernique comparison inequality (Theorem 2.2.3 in \cite{AdlerTaylor2007}) and the fact that
$\nnorm{\texttt{P}_X^{\perp}}_2 \leq 1$. Choosing $t = (1 + \sqrt{2}) \sigma \{w(\mc{T}) \vee \log n \}$, combining this result with i), and putting together the pieces in \eqref{eq:Pi_apply_Gordon}, the assertion of the lemma follows.

